<p><code>Pop\Application</code> decides which router to build by looking at how PHP was invoked, so nothing in that
script says &quot;this is CLI&quot;. The route table is what makes it a console application:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><span class="code-file">app/config/app.cli.php</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">&lt;?php
</span><span class="text-kw">return</span> [
    <span class="text-str">&#039;routes&#039;</span> =&gt; [
        <span class="text-str">&#039;users list [--limit=]&#039;</span> =&gt; [
            <span class="text-str">&#039;controller&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-str">&#039;App\Console\Controller\UsersController&#039;</span>,
            <span class="text-str">&#039;action&#039;</span>     =&gt; <span class="text-str">&#039;index&#039;</span>,
